			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Strip Effect Layer wrappers from 18 workbench live implementations\n\nRemove the `Layer.succeed` / `Layer` import indirection layer from all workbench service live implementations — UserSettings, Activity, Clipboard, Command, ContextKey, Dialog, Editor, Extension, Host, Keybinding, Layout, Lifecycle, Notification, Product, Progress, Storage, Theme, and Workspace — replacing `export const XLive = Layer.succeed(Tag, makeX())` with direct `export const XLive = makeX()`.\n\nThis is the second wave of the Layer-flattening initiative (following 8814bfe1). Each file also drops the unused `Layer` import and the corresponding `*ServiceTag` import. The factory function `makeX()` already produces a valid service object matching its interface; wrapping it in a `Layer` provided no additional composition value since these services are consumed directly via the tag in Wind's dependency graph.\n\nRemoves 72 lines of boilerplate across 18 files. All exports remain available as named and default exports for backward compatibility.",
			"SHA": "baabb3fa4406f6dcd2f875658d0d27b73fefbf79"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:05:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				924,
				11
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Flatten Effect wrappers and harden Tauri IPC dispatch\n\nRemove indirection from editor state management, progress reporter, and text model resolver by replacing `Ref`/`Effect.runFork` with direct mutable variables and sync calls where asynchronous wrapping added no value. Simultaneously strengthen the Tauri IPC layer with proper listener lifecycle tracking, reliable node-deferred fallback, and error propagation.\n\n**Editor state (Live.ts):** Replace `Ref.unsafeMake`/`Ref.set`/`Ref.get` wrapping with bare `let`/`const` variables and `Effect.sync` accessors. The Tauri event listener subscription shifts from `Effect.runFork`/`Effect.promise` to raw `async`/`await import`, removing the imperative Effect allocation around a fundamentally imperative callback.\n\n**Progress service (WorkbenchProgressLive/Interface):** Make `Report` a sync `void` return — the upstream VS Code reporter is already synchronous — and change `Run`'s body callback to `Promise<A>` instead of `Effect.Effect<A, …>`. The bridge API (`window.createAsyncWorkbenchProgress`) expects an async function, so wrapping its return in `Effect.runPromise` was pure overhead.\n\n**Text model resolver (TextModelResolver/Live):** Replace `Effect.runFork` + `Effect.ignoreLogged` with `Effect.runPromise` + `.catch(() => {})`, avoiding a forked fiber with logged-ignore semantics for a fire-and-forget close.\n\n**Tauri IPC (TauriIPC.ts):** Implement proper `ChannelUnlisteners` tracking in a module-level `Map<string, () => void[]>` so that `removeAllListeners` actually detaches Tauri event listeners instead of accumulating them across window reloads. Fix `send` to always serialize args as `unknown[]` — prior special-casing of single-element arrays caused Mountain-side argument desync with TauriMainProcessService's contract.\n\n**Tauri main process service (TauriMainProcessService.ts):**\n- Remove `output` from `FireAndForgetChannels`: Mountain's `output:createOutputChannel` and `registerLogger` return handles that callers consume, so they must round-trip.\n- Add `NodeDeferred` tier: when Mountain returns `undefined` (no native handler registered) or throws, the call re-dispatches through the Node-tier cocoon:request path instead of surfacing the error or returning `undefined` to undefined-intolerant workbench consumers.\n- Propagate MistWS errors: instead of silently catching and falling back to Mountain, `Node`-tier calls now rethrow the error to maintain the Node-only contract. Other tiers trace the double-dispatch.\n- Rethrow Mountain invocation errors instead of returning `undefined`: callers expecting arrays or tuples see a rejected promise rather than `undefined` leaking into `.map`/`.forEach`.\n\n**Storage (StorageService Live/Interface):** Add `GetItems` (bulk read as `[key, value][]` tuples), `UpdateItems` (atomic insert/delete in one round-trip), and `Optimize` (flush the store) — wiring three new IPC channels against Mountain's `StorageProvider`.\n\n**Search (SearchService Live/Interface):** Accept `string | readonly string[]` for `include`/`exclude` glob patterns and normalize to `string[]` via `ToGlobArray` before sending to Mountain, matching the workbench's dual single-string/array contract.\n\n**Workspaces (Live.ts):** Extract inline coercion logic into a named `CoerceFolderArray` helper for readability.",
			"SHA": "8814bfe130f9dbe578f886694c4cb249d3c5e427"
		},
